the family of a georgia woman missing  since 2005  is waiting for a state supreme court  ruling that would allow a long-awaited  murder trial to go forward  after tara grinstead disappeared her  case remained unsolved for nearly 12  years  but authorities may have missed leads  that potentially could have solved the  case  soon after she vanished peter van sant  reports for this week's 48 hours  from the day tara grinstead disappeared  from her home in 2005  the small town of ocilla georgia has  been consumed with one question  what really happened to tara grinstead  neighbor  janice polk tara grinstad was a  very well liked high school teacher tara  also competed in beauty pageants  later mentoring other young women that's  what she was doing on the morning of  october 22nd  2005 the day she disappeared  recalls her best friend maria woods  harbor  and after the pageant she went to a  cookout went home  and then nobody's seen her since  for years the case remained a mystery  but this man john mccullough says that  back in 2007  he tried to share with authorities  information that he believed  could have solved the case he says a  buddy he met in the army  named bo dukes told him he knew who  killed tara  he had told me that his friend  accidentally strangled her  and he needed help getting rid of the  body so you called the police department  this is john mccullough i know who  killed tara grinstead  does anyone call you back no but a  decade later  this woman brook sheridan came forward  with a similar story  also from beau dukes then her boyfriend  beau told her his friend ryan duke had  murdered tara  during a robbery the two men had similar  names  but were not related he said i can't  handle it anymore and he starts telling  me everything  beau told brook that he had nothing to  do with tara's death  but had helped his friend ryan burn  tara's body  in a pecan orchard i said you need to  confess  you need to own up to what you've done  and confess based on what beau told  investigators  ryan duke was arrested for grinstead's  murder  he pleaded not guilty and is awaiting  trial  in march 2019 beau dukes was convicted  on charges relating  to covering up the crime and sentenced  to 25 years in prison  but tara's friend maria believes that  the whole truth  hasn't been told i believe  that ryan and bo duke were both in this  together  peter van sant joins us now good morning  what a story how are you this morning  i'm good i'm good i'm alive so i'm good  amen so tell us what is ryan duke side  of the story  well ryan's story has evolved back in  2017  according to the georgia bureau of  investigation he allegedly  confessed to killing tara he said he was  high on drugs when he entered her home  to steal her purse but now his defense  attorneys have publicly said that that  confession  is false and at trial they plan on  pointing the finger of blame at beau  dukes  even though there is no physical  evidence that beau committed the murder  and that latex glove that was found on  terrace property  has ryan's dna inside it  so with all the tips that came in after  her death what happened to them  this is so frustrating you heard john  mccullough uh  he's he's just tormented by this well it  turns out several weeks after tara's  disappearance there was a second tipster  who overheard  bo and ryan talk about the crime  implicating  themselves so he also contacted  authorities  but sadly no one properly followed up  on these tips in a case that could have  been solved  in a matter of weeks instead of many  years  peter van san thank you so much you can  see peter's report that tara grinstead  mystery on 48 hours  this saturday at 10 9 central right here  on cbs
 

